INSERT INTO `grupo_en` VALUES
(1,1,'National Theater Coordination','cnt.jpg',NULL,'<p>It has the mission of encouraging innovative processes through professional theater programs aimed at diverse audiences. The Coordination collaborates with theater communities to provide professional and creative development opportunities. Its work reflects complexity, disrupts assumptions, welcomes diversity, and amplifies joy.</p>',NULL,'wcrwrnM2h3o',1,'2022-09-13 18:36:31','2022-09-21 18:55:32'),
(2,1,'National Theater Company','cnteatro.jpg',NULL,'<p>Its goal is to develop high-quality theatrical productions that can be performed in Mexico and abroad. In the last ten years, it has premiered more than 70 plays by diverse playwrights, mainly Mexicans. The Company has performed plays from different eras and places: Ibero-American Costumbrismo, Russian Realism, French Classicism, Spanish Golden Age, Elizabethan Theater, Contemporary German Theater, Experimental Theater, among many others. Through the art of theater, it provides cultural enrichment, creative development, and opportunities for self-discovery. The Company celebrates diversity and honors our cultural heritage.</p>','',NULL,1,'2022-09-16 19:39:59','2022-09-23 10:28:27'),
(3,2,'National Dance Coordination','cnd.jpg',NULL,'<p>Its goal is, on the one hand, to encourage professional dance-developing mechanisms to promote creator’s involvement in dance productions and training activities; on the other hand, it inspires a lasting love and appreciation for dance through artistic excellence, high-quality performances, innovative choreographies, and educational activities. The Coordination’s mission is to enrich its audiences by sharing the power and joy of dance and broadening the reach and impact of dance through active community engagement.</p>','',NULL,1,'2022-09-16 19:43:52','2022-09-23 10:33:18'),
(4,2,'National Dance Company','cndanza.jpg',NULL,'<p>Founded in 1977, it is a classical ballet company made up of 72 dancers which promote and preserve works from the classical, neoclassical, and contemporary repertoires. This mission is accompanied by a commitment to expand the Company\'s audience and make ballet accessible to the widest possible public through touring, the creative use of media, and other outreach efforts.</p>','<p>Classical repertoire</p><p></p><ul><li><i>Don Quixote (Suite) </i>– Choreography by Marius Petipa.<br>Adaptation and Replacement: Cuauhtémoc Nájera and the Company\'s teachers.</li><li><i>Miliano </i>- Choreography by Irina Marcano</li><li><i>Suite from Swan Lake</i> - Choreography by Cuauhtémoc Nájera and Sonia Jiménez.</li><li><i>Planimetry of movement</i> - Choreography by Irina Marcano.</li><li><i>Romanza</i> - Choreography by James Kelly.</li><li><i>All long dem day</i> - Choreography by Marco Goecke.</li></ul><p>International tours</p><p></p><ul><li><i>Por vos muero</i> - Choreography by Nacho Duato.</li><li><i>Romanza</i> - Choreography by James Kelly.</li><li><i>Planimetry of movement </i>- Choreography by Irina Marcano.</li><li><i>The Emerald </i>- Choreography by Agrippina Vaganova.</li><li><i>Casta Diva</i> - Choreography by Yazmín Barragán.</li><li><i>Swan Lake Suite</i> - Choreography by Cuauhtémoc Nájera &amp; Sonia Jiménez.</li><li><i>La Bayadera</i> - Choreography by Marius Petipa.</li><li><i>All long dem day</i> - Choreography by Marco Goecke.</li></ul><p></p>',NULL,1,'2022-09-16 19:47:47','2022-09-24 02:25:02'),
(5,2,'Contemporary Dance Production Center','ceprodac.jpg',NULL,'<p>Founded in 2011, it is comprised of 20 professional contemporary dancers. Its goal is to enrich, expand, and excel in the art of contemporary dance through world-class performances, high-caliber choreographic creations, and impactful engagement to expand the Ceprodac\'s audience and make contemporary dance accessible to the widest possible public.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-16 19:51:39','2022-09-23 11:34:04'),
(6,3,'National Coordination of Music and Opera','cnmo.jpg',NULL,'<p>Its aim is to provide welcoming, accessible, and high-quality music experiences for its audiences. The Coordination’s goal is to foster the world’s musical legacy, while recognizing traditional and avant-garde aesthetics. It advances the enjoyment of music, promotes music appreciation, and supports emerging Mexican talent.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-16 19:53:49','2022-09-23 11:34:07'),
(7,3,'National Symphony Orchestra','osn.jpg',NULL,'<p>Founded by Carlos Chávez in 1928, it is the most important orchestral ensemble in Mexico. Its repertoire ranges from works from the Baroque period to Contemporary compositions. Its goal is to inspire audiences through exceptional orchestral performances and programs.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-16 19:56:49','2022-09-23 11:34:12'),
(8,3,'Chamber Orchestra of <i>Bellas Artes</i>','ocba.jpg',NULL,'<p>The Orchestra strives to cultivate an appreciation for chamber music through quality concerts that can be performed both within and outside of Mexico. It consists of 23 musicians, and its repertoire includes primarily Mexican, and Latin American music, as well as European compositions that span more than three Centuries.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-16 19:59:35','2022-09-23 11:34:16'),
(9,3,'Contemporary Music Experimentation and Production Center','cepromusic.jpg',NULL,'<p>Founded in 2012, the Cepromusic Ensemble is devoted to the promotion of high-quality contemporary music. It performs the most significant music of our time, from masterworks of the 20th Century to the most recent works of this Century. It also carries out academic activities focused on experimentation, production, and training. The Ensemble’s mission is accompanied by a commitment to make contemporary music accessible to the widest possible public through the creative use of media, and other outreach efforts.</p>','',NULL,1,'2022-09-16 20:01:39','2022-09-23 12:15:46'),
(10,4,'National Opera Company','opera.jpg',NULL,'<p>The Company’s goal is to thrill, inspire and educate through the shared experience of opera. It is devoted to deliver outstanding productions of traditional and new repertoires that engage the public and propel the genre forward. Through its innovative programming, it underscores compositions by Mexican authors, and endeavors to broaden and diversify the opera audience.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-16 20:04:34','2022-09-23 11:34:23'),
(11,4,'Studio of the <i>Bellas Artes</i> Opera (EOBA) ','eoba.jpg',NULL,'<p>Mexico\'s most important center for opera professionalization. It fosters the artistic development of young professional singers and pianists through master classes with high-level international singers, conductors, and operatic ambassadors. The Studio hosts twelve singers and two pianists every year.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-16 20:07:30','2022-09-23 11:34:27'),
(12,5,'National Coordination of Literature','cnl.jpg',NULL,'<p>Its mission is to foster the professional development of writers, to promote communication throughout the literary community, and to help create an environment in which literature can be appreciated by the widest possible public through educational activities, festivals, round tables, homages, and exhibitions. The Coordination strives to celebrate the best literature in Mexico. The <i>Bellas Artes</i> Literary Awards and additional programming encourage existing readers and build new and diverse audiences.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-17 00:30:49','2022-09-23 11:34:30'),
(13,5,'Cultural Extension Program','extension.jpg',NULL,'<p>Books and literature are for everyone, no matter where the reader is situated geographically, economically, racially, or otherwise. Cultural Extension’s activities promote the habit of reading, with the intent of awakening curiosity, empathy, and an interest in literature, particularly in texts written by Mexican authors.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-17 00:35:05','2022-09-23 11:34:32'),
(14,7,'Social Inclusion, Diversity, and Equality','inclusion.jpg',NULL,'<p>The Program’s goal is to generate actions related to accessibility, non-discrimination, cultural diversity, and gender equality.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2022-09-17 00:37:59','2022-09-23 11:34:35');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `grupo_en` ENABLE KEYS */;
