INSERT INTO `programas_en` VALUES
(1,1,1,'<b>National School Theater Program</b>','cnt/tescolar.jpg','<p>This project is part of a set of initiatives to promote artistic education and social inclusion, thus contributing to young audience’s development and training. This is carried out in collaboration with local cultural agencies and educational authorities. The productions which emerge from this Program are available for streaming.</p>',1,'2022-09-18 02:26:03','2022-09-24 00:26:06'),
(2,1,1,'<b>Monologue Festival - Theater with one voice</b>','cnt/1voz.jpg','<p>Scenic corridor created to develop one-man shows in Mexico. Created in 2005, every edition generates collaborations and creates new audiences. Furthermore, it brings exposure to local theater companies. In addition, this festival offers professionalization workshops online to encourage the development of local projects, taught by a member of each selected company.</p>',1,'2022-09-20 09:58:31','2022-09-24 00:26:12'),
(3,1,1,'<b>National Theater Showcase</b>','cnt/mnt.jpg','<p>Itinerant event that is held annually, every November. Each edition is co-produced in collaboration with a different State, allowing a nation-wide generation of networks of theater professionals. Its goal is to encourage the participation of creators from all over Mexico, with the intention of generating a training space that guarantees the development of Mexican theater, and the creation of new audiences. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 13:30:06','2022-09-24 00:26:16'),
(4,1,1,'<b>EFITEATRO</b>','cnt/efiteatro.jpg','<p>Fiscal stimulus intended for businesses to foment investment in national theatrical productions. The Coordination distributes the General Rules among the performing arts communities and carries out informative talks and workshops to facilitate the application process.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 13:30:32','2022-09-24 00:26:23'),
(5,1,1,'<b>National Theater Congress</b>','cnt/congT.jpg','<p>It consists of round tables that are held both via streaming and in-person aiming at exchanging ideas among the theater community. </p>',1,'2022-09-23 13:30:54','2022-09-24 00:26:28'),
(6,1,1,'<b>Prison Theater Contest</b>','cnt/tpenit.jpg','<p>Organized in collaboration with the Secretariat of Security and Civilian Protection of Mexico, it encourages playwriting among the prison population. At the end of the contest, three selected texts are produced to be performed.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 13:31:32','2022-09-24 00:26:33'),
(7,1,1,'<b>Centro Cultural del Bosque</b>','cnt/ccb.jpg','<p>This cultural hub offers a regular theater programming (for all ages), previously selected each year via national open calls. The performances are presented in the following venues: <br></p><ul><li>Del Bosque (Julio Castillo) Theater</li><li>Xavier Villaurrutia Hall</li><li>El Galeón (Abraham Oceransky) Theater</li><li>El Granero (Xavier Rojas) Theater</li><li>“Luisa Josefina Hernández” Orientación Theater</li><li>Angel Salas Square</li><p></p></ul>',1,'2022-09-23 13:32:58','2022-09-24 00:26:38'),
(8,1,2,'<b><i>El Diccionario / The Dictionary</i></b><br /><h4>By Manuel Calzada Pérez<br />Director: Enrique Singer</h4>','cnteatro/diccionario.jpg','<p>A play about the arduous efforts of librarian and philologist María Moliner, author of El diccionario del uso español, who throughout 15 years of meticulous work done alone in her home, captured definitions, synonyms, and meanings of different expressions and phrases of common usage, leaving a valuable legacy on the Spanish language as well as a testimony to the rigor and excellence of her work.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 14:30:59','2022-09-24 02:04:10'),
(9,1,2,'<b><i>El convivio del difunto</i> / The Dead Man’s Party</b><br /><h4>Script and direction: Martín Zapata</h4>','cnteatro/difunto.jpg','<p>Leonor, a refined aristocrat, has lost her husband. Well, she hasn\'t lost him completely, only kind of. That is, Mauricio, her husband, is dead, but he is still talking and moving. Why? Nobody knows. But faced with this extraordinary situation, Leonor seeks comfort in her two best friends. Magda, the maid, serves some drinks by order of Mauricio, and that is how the party of the dead man begins, to which, of course, we are all invited. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 14:37:53','2022-09-24 02:04:24'),
(10,1,2,'<b><i>DeSazón</i></b><br /><h4>By Víctor Hugo Rascón Banda <br />Based on the original idea by José Caballero and Alejandro Luna</h4>','cnteatro/desazon.jpg','<p>Three women, native of Chihuahua, talk and cook memories. Survivors of loneliness, marginalization, courage, and conviction, María Müller (a Mennonite), Consuelo Armenta (a woman from the Chihuahua highlands) and Amanda Campos (dressed in Tarahumara indigenous clothing), share what their lives have been like in a land where the borders of religion, language, drug trafficking, and guerrilla warfare stand like granite walls, while they find a way to move forward. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 21:54:42','2022-09-24 02:05:41'),
(11,1,2,'<b><i>Conferencia sobre la lluvia</i> / A Conference On Rain</b><br /><h4>By Juan Villoro<br />Director: Sandra Félix</h4>','cnteatro/confelluvia.jpg','<p>A librarian is going to give a lecture on the relationship between rain and romantic poetry, but he loses his papers and ends up making a crazy personal confession. The subject of this play is love and reading<br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 22:56:16','2022-09-24 02:05:02'),
(12,1,2,'<b><i>¡Violencia! / Violence!</i></b><br /><h4>By Valeria Loera<br />Director: Diana Sedano</h4>','cnteatro/violencia.jpg','<p>After a heartbreak, Violencia López decides to lock herself in her house -and in her thoughts- to cohabit with her multiple Violencias and with the ghost of her deceased father, treating herself with violence and immersing herself in her own misery, until the arrival of her mother, who comes with devastating news and an unexpected and perverse gift... but which is just what Violencia needs. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 23:01:16','2022-09-24 02:05:17'),
(13,1,2,'<b><i>Las visiones / The Visions</i></b><br /><h4>By José Emilio Hernández<br />Director: Boris Schoemann</h4>','cnteatro/visiones.jpg','<p>Ramón Llanes and Atanasio Robles are searching for Francisco Villa. They say he is in Canatlán. Margarita and Catalina Macías try to keep up with them. Time stretches out, stops, and becomes irrelevant. The country becomes a puzzle to be deciphered in dreams and in the marks left by the stones on the road. Love in times of the Mexican Revolution is not what it seems. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 23:46:27','2022-09-24 02:06:13'),
(14,1,2,'<b><i>Olvida todo / Forget Everything</i></b><br /><h4>By Ximena Escalante<br />Director: Mariana Hartasánchez</h4>','cnteatro/olvidatodo.jpg','<p>On the night of September 29, 1968, Elena Garro is kidnapped for a few hours by Socrates, leader of the student movement. On her return, Elena takes refuge in a friend\'s boarding house downtown.&nbsp; There, and throughout that night until dawn, Elena gets help by the residents of the decadent boarding house to change her appearance for her to flee the country. In those stormy hours, Elena manufactures the decline of her successful literary career by entering the tunnels of a political plot where she is pursued by both the rebel movement and the government, who accuse her of being a spy. Thus, while the army and the police wait for her behind the door of the boarding house, a ghostly Elena self-fictionalizes her new character, lost between the time of her stories and a city that turns its back on her.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-23 23:51:55','2022-09-24 02:06:30'),
(15,2,3,'<b>Peninsular and/or Regional Meeting</b>','cnd/peninsular.jpg','<p>The Coordination collaborates with local and regional agents to design a wide range of activities. This kind of practices and interactive processes attempt to involve audiences and communities as much as possible, considering the context and the territory.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 00:01:20','2022-09-24 00:47:39'),
(16,2,3,'<b>Training and knowledge sharing</b>','cnd/formacion.jpg','<p>The exchange of knowledge and network strengthening are achieved through the following mechanisms: </p><ul><li>Colloquiums, certifications, workshops, talks, seminars, and micro-laboratories.</li><li>Alliances with cultural and educational institutions through collaborative work. </li><li>Promotion of independent private, public, autonomous or community venues.</li><li>Utilization of new technologies, digital tools, and transdisciplinary processes.<br><br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-24 00:04:04','2022-09-24 00:47:46'),
(17,2,3,'<b>Encuentro Nacional de Danza (ENDMéxico) / National Dance Meeting</b>','cnd/end.jpg','<p>ENDMéxico is a platform which brings visibility to national dance professionals and their creations. There is a convergence and dialogue related to the diversity of existing practices from all over Mexico. The exchange of knowledge is highly promoted as well as the creation of networks among the participants.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 01:21:31','2022-09-24 01:40:52'),
(18,2,3,'<b>“Guillermo Arriaga\" National Dance Award. INBAL-UAM Contemporary Choreographic Creation Contest</b>','cnd/premioarriaga.jpg','<p>The award’s purpose is to encourage contemporary choreographic creation in Mexico, offering recognition to artists.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 01:26:51','2022-09-24 01:47:39'),
(19,2,3,'<b>Artistic programming at the Centro Cultural del Bosque (CCB) and alternative venues</b>','cnd/teatrodanza.jpg','<p>Dance performances are presented in the following venues: </p><ul><li>“Guillermina Bravo” Dance Theater (CCB).</li><li>Ángel Salas Square (CCB).</li><li>La Caja.</li><li>Los Pinos Cultural Center.</li><li>Markets and public spaces in Mexico City.</li><li>Mexico City’s Metro System</li><li>Cultural spaces run independently, or by public institutions.<br><br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-24 01:28:51','2022-09-24 01:41:33'),
(20,2,3,'<b>International Dance Day</b>','cnd/did.jpg','<p>UNESCO proposed this day to be celebrated every April 29th. On this holiday, choreographers, dancers, and performers come together to honor the discipline through diverse activities such as performances and training workshops.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 01:32:07','2022-09-24 01:41:40'),
(21,2,3,'<b>National Performing Arts Circuit: Dance and Self-Managed Spaces</b>','cnd/circuito.jpg','<p>The goal is to present a selection of performances in regional cultural circuits which, in turn, are expected to reinforce ties between artists, cultural agents, and self-managed spaces in different regions of Mexico. This initiative seeks to decentralize cultural processes in the country.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 01:35:06','2022-09-24 01:43:18'),
(22,2,3,'<b>EFIDANZA</b>','cnd/efidanza.jpg','<p>Fiscal stimulus intended for businesses to foment investment in national dance productions. The Coordination distributes the General Rules among the performing arts communities and carries out informative talks and workshops to facilitate the application process.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 02:00:03','2022-09-24 02:11:24'),
(23,2,4,'<b>Don Quixote (Suite),<br />Program I</b>','cndanza/quijote.jpg','<p>In a marketplace, Don Quixote and Sancho Panza wander among the colorful crowd. Kitri, daughter of the innkeeper Lorenzo, and her fiancé, the barber Basilio, are in it. The lovers\' rendezvous is suddenly interrupted by her father, who introduces her to the rich old Gamache, as the fiancé he has chosen for her. They, in vain, make plans since Lorenzo is adamant on the wedding. Don Quixote, who thinks he recognizes his beloved Dulcinea in Kitri, intervenes and helps them flee. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 02:03:58','2022-09-24 02:18:08'),
(24,2,4,'<b>Company\'s Evening Gala, Program II</b>','cndanza/lago.jpg','<p>This program is integrated by pieces such as: S<i>uite (from Swan Lake), Planimetry of Movement, Romanza, All long dem day and Miliano</i>, combined with new creations of the Company made by their members and by guest choreographers.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 02:12:37','2022-09-24 02:23:58'),
(25,2,4,'<b>International Gala</b>','cndanza/romanza.jpg','<p>This program consists of works such as: I Die for You, Romanza, Planimetry of Movement, The Emerald, Casta Diva, the Suite from The Swan Lake, La Bayadère, and All long dem day. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-24 02:15:05','2022-09-24 02:24:02'),
(26,2,5,'<b>On-site repertoire</b>','ceprodac/signos.jpg','<ul><li><i>Signs, the Body of the Night (Signos, el cuerpo de la noche),</i> by Óscar Ruvalcaba</li><li><i>Sonorous Light: Celebrating Mario Lavista (Luz Sonora. Celebrando a Mario Lavista),</i> dir. Claudia Lavista</li><li><i>Contemporary Dance Gala (Gala de Danza Contemporánea),</i> dir. Cecilia Lugo Lyrics, Dance, and Music Sheets (Letra, danza y partitura, dir. Cecilia Lugo (starting on the second half of 2023)</li><li><i>Stories from the 5th Sun (Historias del 5to Sol), </i>dir. Cecilia Lugo (starting on the second half of 2023)<br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-26 09:45:54','2022-09-26 15:57:49'),
(27,2,5,'<b>Video-dances and virtual repertoire</b>','ceprodac/heroes.jpg','<ul><li><i>Heroes (Héroes),</i> by Lidya Romero</li><li><i>Sor Juana 325 / The Feeling of Being Absent (Sor Juana 325 / Sentimientos de ausente)</i><br>Conmemorates the 325th anniversary of this Mexican writer’s death. </li><li><i>Geography in Movement (Geografía en movimiento)</i><br>Conmemorates seven outstanding personalities of Mexican contemporary dance, and it is performed within INBAL’s 75th anniversary celebration. </li><li><i>From the Root to the Flower (De la raíz a la flor)</i><br>Performed within the International Decade of Indigenous Languages celebration of 2022-2032 (Decenio Internacional de las Lenguas Indígenas 2022-2032)</li></ul>',1,'2022-09-26 09:52:21','2022-09-26 15:57:56'),
(28,2,5,'<b>Other activities</b>','ceprodac/formacion.jpg','<p>Lectures, conferences, workshops, courses, and in-person and virtual master classes on: </p><ul><li>Contemporary dance</li><li>Theatrical mechanics and lighting</li><li>Cultural communication</li><li>Stage production</li><li>Art and migration<br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-26 09:56:48','2022-09-26 15:58:07'),
(29,3,6,'<b>44<sup>th</sup> “Manuel Enriquez” International Forum for New Music (FIMNME)</b>','cnmo/finmne.jpg','<p>International showcase for the new generations of creators (orchestras, ensembles, and soloists) from all over Mexico and the world. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:01:16','2022-09-26 15:58:56'),
(30,3,6,'<b>10<sup>th</sup> National Piano Competition “Angelica Morales – Yamaha”</b>','cnmo/yamaha.jpg','<p>It has positioned itself as the most important piano competition in Mexico. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:03:06','2022-09-26 15:59:47'),
(31,3,6,'<b>IBERMUSICAS</b>','cnmo/ibermusicas.jpg','<p>It is an international cooperation program aiming at music professionals. It promotes the presence and recognition of Ibero-American musical diversity. There are currently 12 countries that are part of the program: Argentina, Chile, Colombia, Costa Rica, Cuba, Ecuador, Mexico, Panama, Paraguay, Peru, Portugal, and Uruguay. Songwriting and musical composition contests will be launched in the coming months. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:04:09','2022-09-26 15:59:51'),
(32,3,6,'<b>EFIMUSICA</b>','cnmo/efimusica.jpg','<p>Fiscal stimulus intended for businesses to foment investment in music related projects. The Coordination distributes the General Rules among the performing arts communities and carries out informative talks and workshops to facilitate the application process.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:06:18','2022-09-26 16:04:23'),
(33,3,6,'<b>Concert performers of <i>Bellas Artes</i></b>','cnmo/concertistas.jpg','<p>Artistic group comprised of 48 high-level musicians, respectively specialized in piano, guitar, violin, viola, cello, woodwinds, harp, and voice. They can perform in the following formats: solos, duos, quartets, quintets, and perform concerts as soloists with an orchestral accompaniment. They also organize didactic concerts, workshops, and master classes, and serve as jurors in music competitions.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:09:08','2022-09-26 16:01:51'),
(34,3,6,'<b>Solo singers</b>','cnmo/solistas.jpg','<p>It is composed of 20 soprano, mezzo-soprano, tenor, and baritone singers. They perform chamber music concerts, voice, and piano duets, as well as didactic concerts as part of the program <i>El Arte del canto (The Art of Singing)</i>, which for 31 years has brought the lyrical art to middle and high school students. </p><p>Through programs such as <i>Conciertos de Bellas Artes</i> and<i> Bellas Artes a todas partes</i>, the singers bring concerts to locations all around Mexico and abroad. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:12:19','2022-09-26 16:01:55'),
(35,3,6,'<b><i>Bellas Artes</i> Ensamble of Solois</b>t<br />Artistic director: Christian Gohmer','cnmo/solistasensamble.jpg','<p>Founded in 1984 by Rufino Montero, it has had as guest conductors Erika Kubacsek, James Demster, Horacio Franco, Josep Cabré, Maurizio Baldin, Pablo Varela, and Xavier Ribes. The group focuses on a diverse repertoire, ranging from oratorio to chamber opera and operetta. The ensemble has recorded the works of Mexican composers such as Blas Galindo, Carlos Chávez, and Silvestre Revueltas. In the last four years it has staged three chamber operas.</p><p><b>PROGRAMS</b></p><ul><li><b>American Vocal Music </b><br>It includes pieces by major American composers from the first half of the last century, including Gershwin, and Hamilton. This program attempts to articulate a mix between African-American music and the representatives of what is considered to be refined music.</li><li><b>Gianni Schicchi by Giacomo Puccini</b> <br>It is an opera in one act that explores the characters\' reactions to the possibility of receiving an inheritance. This staging offers a modern interpretation and current outlook to the audience. </li><li><b>Renaissance Polyphony: Orlando di Lasso</b> <br>A program based entirely on Orlando di Lasso (a French-Flemish Renaissance musician) compositions. It aims to bring the audience closer to European polyphonic music.<br><br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-26 10:15:55','2022-09-26 16:01:46'),
(36,3,6,'<b>Madrigalists Choir</b><br />Artistic director: Carlos Aransay','cnmo/madrigalistas.jpg','<p>Founded in 1938 by Luis Sandi, its objective is to disseminate choral music. It has an extensive repertoire ranging from the first musical manifestations in the West to contemporary vocal pieces. </p><p><b>PROGRAMS</b></p><ul><li><i><b>Voces con sentido – lenguas y músicas de México / Voices with meaning - Languages and music from Mexico</b></i><br>Choral works sung in different native languages and while animated indigenous stories from the 68 voices 68 hearts are projected to the audience. It includes the participation of guest traditional musicians.</li><li><b>Three friends: Schütz, Schein and Scheidt </b><br>The program includes sacred and madrigal music compositions, and introduces the most important works of baroque composers, including Johann Hermann Schein, Samuel Scheidt, and Heinrich Schütz (who were friends). The latter is recognized and remembered as one of the great composers of the 17th century.</li><li><b>Pilgrimage on the road to Santiago</b> <br>This program presents pilgrims\' songs recorded in different manuscripts, for example the Calixtino Codex, the Llibre Vermell de Montserrat, the Las Huelgas Codex and the Cantigas de Santa María (attributed to Alfonso X the Wise and his court, where the Virgin Mary intercedes for the health and forgiveness in the penitence of the pilgrims).<br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-26 10:22:55','2022-09-26 16:02:00'),
(37,3,7,'<b>Collaborations</b>','osn/colabora.jpg','<p>In addition to its annual Concert Seasons at the Palacio de Bellas Artes in Mexico City, the Orchestra has the opportunity of collaborating with musical institutions from different regions of Mexico, be it through the staging of concerts or in music education activities. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:30:11','2022-09-26 16:02:50'),
(38,3,7,'<b>Educational activities</b>','osn/edu.jpg','<p>The Orchestra has teachers with a long pedagogical trajectory in its ranks. They perform alongside Chamber Music Ensembles, orchestras and music schools located throughout Mexico, either in-person or broadcasted virtually. These concerts are usually preceded by lectures, workshops, or master classes. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:31:37','2022-09-26 16:02:56'),
(39,3,8,'<b>Activities</b>','ocba/actividades.jpg','<ul><li>Broadcasts of performances from the 2021 Concert Season.</li><li>Virtual pedagogical activities hosted by the Orchestra’s director, Ludwig Carrasco, aimed at collaborating with young musicians from all the states of Mexico (e.g., master classes, workshops, courses). These activities are focused on Chamber Music, Conducting, and Opera.<br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-26 10:33:47','2022-09-26 16:05:08'),
(40,3,9,'<b>Seasonal Concerts</b><br />José Luis Castillo, artistic director','cepromusic/temporada.jpg','<p>A series of concerts that feature the most representative repertoire from the XX and XXI Centuries.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:37:49','2022-09-26 16:07:48'),
(41,3,9,'<b>Interdisciplinary activities</b>','cepromusic/interdis.jpg','<p>Radio concerts, recitals, and artistic activities in collaboration with Visual Arts, Theater, Dance, Silent Cinema, and Photography professionals.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:39:01','2022-09-26 16:07:53'),
(42,3,9,'<b>Special Concerts</b>','cepromusic/especiales.jpg','<p>The Chamber Music Series <i>Aliqua</i>, and the <i>Impropia</i> Series (with improvisational works or concerts), are concerts related to a range of topics such as migration, gender, among others.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:41:08','2022-09-26 16:26:40'),
(43,3,9,'<b>Educational</b>','cepromusic/formacion.jpg','<p>Master classes, conferences, round tables, interviews, and instrumental technique workshops. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 10:42:22','2022-09-26 16:08:11'),
(44,3,9,'<b>Educational and artistic activities across the States</b>','cepromusic/formavirtual.jpg','<p>Festivals, concerts, and artistic residencies in collaborations with other cultural institutions.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 11:00:39','2022-09-26 16:08:54'),
(45,3,9,'<b>International presence</b>','cepromusic/internacional.jpg','<p>The Ensemble has had concerts, Chamber Opera recitals, artistic residencies, workshops, commissions, and masterclasses in collaboration with international musicians such as Christian Wolff, Arditti Quartet, White Noise Collective, David Dove, James Dillon, Kaija Saariaho, Ute Wassermann, Wade Matthews, Tony Arnold Pascal Contet, Sigma Project Quartet, etc.</p><p>It also has teamed up with guest conductors and been benefited by the Permanent Program to Support Young Composers (<i>Programa Permanente de Fortalecimiento a Jóvenes Compositores</i>), where composers from across the nation participate in the creation process and performance of artistic works, and in educational activities. <br><br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 11:02:58','2022-09-26 16:28:01'),
(46,3,9,'<b>Involvement in contemporany music festivals</b>','cepromusic/festivales.jpg','<ul><li><i>Cervantino</i> International Festival </li><li><i>Manuel Enríquez</i> International New Music Forum </li><li>Guanajuato’s International Festival <i>Callejón del Ruido </i></li><li>Querétaro’s <i>Festival Interciclos </i></li><li>Baja California’s <i>Festival de octubre </i></li><li>Veracruz’s International Festival <i>Camerata 21 </i></li><li>International Radio Biennial </li><li>International Contemporary Music Biennial<br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-26 11:07:41','2022-09-26 16:30:39'),
(47,4,10,'<b>Orchestra of the <i>Bellas Artes</i> Theater</b>','opera/otba.jpg','<p>Consisting of 72 musicians, the Orchestra specializes in operatic and ballet repertoire, and a wide selection of the symphonic-vocal repertoire. It was founded in 1955 and, since then, its primary mission has been to take part in the opera and ballet Seasons of the National Institute of the Fine Artes and Literature in collaboration with numerous high-level conductors of national and international prestige. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 11:11:16','2022-09-26 16:10:13'),
(48,4,10,'<b>Choir of the <i>Bellas Artes</i> Theater</b>','opera/coroba.jpg','<p>With 74 members in its ranks, this is a choir specialized in the operatic repertoire, as well as in the symphonic-vocal repertoire. The energy, color, and vocal excellence of its members make it into a choral-lyrical group of the highest quality worldwide.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-26 11:12:43','2022-09-26 16:16:43'),
(49,4,11,'<b>Standard concerts</b>','opera/regulares.jpg','<p><b>Rossini\'s Opera Arias&nbsp; </b></p><p>The program commemorates the 230th anniversary of the composer\'s birth, intended to make his artistic and aesthetic work known among opera audiences. </p><p><i><b>Selections of Mexican opera from the XIX and XX Centuries</b></i></p><p>This program includes Opera Arias by 19th and 20th Centuries Mexican composers such as Melesio Morales, Julio Ituarte, Ricardo Castro, Cenobio Paniagua, among many others. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 00:07:27','2022-09-27 00:55:56'),
(50,5,12,'<b><i>Bellas Artes</i> Literary Awards</b>','literatura/premios.jpg','<ul><li><i>José Revueltas Bellas Artes Award for Literary Essays</i></li><li><i>Edmundo Valadés Bellas Artes Award for Short Fiction </i></li><li><i>Perla Szuchmacher Bellas Artes Award for Theater Plays aimed at Children and Young Audiences </i></li><li><i>Carlos Montemayor Bellas Artes Award for Literary Chronicles </i></li><li><i>Juan Rulfo Bellas Artes Award for Debut Novels&nbsp; </i></li><li><i>Nellie Campobello Bellas Artes Award for Hispanic American Short Stories </i></li><li><i>José Rubén Romero Flores Bellas Artes Award for Full Length Novels </i></li><li><i>Amparo Dávila Bellas Artes Award in San Luis Potosí for Short Stories </i></li><li><i>Juan de la Cabada Bellas Artes Award for Children’s Stories </i></li><li><i>Alfonso Reyes International Award </i></li><li><i>Luisa Josefina Hernández Bellas Artes Award in Baja California for Playwriting </i></li><li><i>Inés Arredondo Bellas Artes Award for Literary Work </i></li><li><i>Buzón Penitenciario Award </i></li><li><i>Carlos Pellicer Bellas Artes Ibero-American Poetry Award for Published Work </i></li><li><i>Bellas Artes Narrative Award in Colima for Published Work (2019) </i></li><li><i>Bellas Artes Award in Aguascalientes for Poetry&nbsp;&nbsp; </i></li><li><i>Xavier Villaurrutia Award from Writers for Writers </i></li><li><i>Juan Ruiz de Alarcón Bellas Artes Award for Playwriting&nbsp; </i></li><li><i>Malcolm Lowry Bellas Artes Award for Literary Essays&nbsp; </i></li><li><i>Margarita Michelena Bellas Artes Award for Literary Translation </i></li><li><i>CaSa Awards 2022 for Literary Works written in Énná (a Mazatec language) </i><br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-27 00:13:38','2022-09-27 00:56:35'),
(51,5,12,'<b>Collections</b>','literatura/libreria.jpg','<p><b>Center for Literary Documentation Casa Leona Vicario</b></p><p>The center archives, safeguards, and disseminates documentary, bibliographic, journalistic, photographic, and audiovisual material about Mexico’s literary life. This collection is available primarily to students and researchers.</p><p><b>Library</b></p><p>It focuses on 20th Century Mexican literature and has a collection of more than 22 thousand copies of diverse narrative texts, poetry, essays, short stories, and plays.</p><p><b>Photographic collection</b></p><p>It consists of around 60 thousand images of contemporary Mexican authors and holds visual record of the activities organized by the Coordination. </p><p><b>The Xavier Villaurrutia Archive</b></p><p>It gathers manuscripts, typewritten original transcripts, notebooks, drawings, photographs, and objects, and serves as evidence of the work of one of the most relevant and influential Mexican writers of the 20th Century, Xavier Villaurrutia. <br><br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 00:29:19','2022-09-27 01:08:39'),
(52,5,12,'<b>The Bio-bibliographic Collection of Mexican Literature</b>','literatura/catalogo.jpg','<p>The electronic version of the Bio-bibliographic Dictionary of Mexican Writers of the 20th Century is now the Bio-bibliographic Collection of Mexican Literature, which has been hosted and available online since 2004 at: </p><p align=\"center\"><a href=\"literatura.inba.gob.mx/catalogo-biobibliografico.html\" target=\"_blank\">literatura.inba.gob.mx/catalogo-biobibliografico.html</a><br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 00:37:15','2022-09-27 01:08:31'),
(53,5,12,'<b>Exhibits</b>','literatura/exhibits.jpg','<p>The Coordination creates exhibits based on its collections. They revolve around the life and work of Mexican authors or, occasionally, on foreign writers living in Mexico. Each one consists mainly of replicas of photographs, documents, and drawings. </p><ul><li><i>Borges in Mexico: A Visual and Literary Chronicle </i></li><li><i>The Present is Perpetual: The Legacy of Octavio Paz (1914-1998) </i></li><li><i>Makers of Stories and Poetry: The Womanly Face of Literature. Photographs by Rogelio Cuéllar </i></li><li><i>The Plaza de Santo Domingo Yesterday, Today and Tomorrow: A Historical Overview </i></li><li><i>Lost Love: Remembering Carlos Monsiváis </i></li><li><i>The Nights of Francisco Tario </i></li><li><i>Facing Poetry: Images of Mexican Poets </i></li><li><i>Benítez in Culture: An Homage to Fernando Benítez </i></li><li><i>Something About Jaime Sabines </i></li><li><i>Andrés Henestrosa: Graphic Memory </i></li><li><i>Gabriel García Márquez and his One Hundred Years of Solitude </i></li><li><i>The Footsteps of Jorge Ibargüengoitia </i></li><li><i>The Image of The Spell – Photographs by Barry Domínguez and Fernando Sánchez</i></li><li><i>Mayáns: Poet, Playwright, Diplomat and Teacher (1925- 2007)</i></li><li><i>A Tribute to Carlos Fuentes. Ten Years After his Departure (2012-2022)</i><br></li></ul>',1,'2022-09-27 00:44:35','2022-09-27 00:59:39'),
(54,5,12,'<b><i>The Alfonsina Chapel</i></b>','literatura/capilla.jpg','<p>The <i>Capilla Alfonsina</i> is a museum and a cultural center that promotes the interest around the life and work of Alfonso Reyes. This is achieved through guided tours, literary activities (conferences, literary cycles, homages, editorial presentations, etc.), courses and workshops, as well as through its library, newspaper catalog, photographic collection, and documentary center. </p><p><b>Guided tours:</b> To talk about The Alfonsina Chapel is to talk about the house where Alfonso Reyes lived for 20 years and where all his memories have been preserved in the form of documents, photographs, furniture, works of art, and diverse objects, representing a portion of the life of the writer and his family.</p><p>Furthermore, the Chapel hosts paintings by Diego Rivera, José Clemente Orozco, Angelina Beloff, Ángel Zárraga, Julio Ruelas, Manuel Rodríguez Lozano, Roberto Montenegro, Héctor Xavier, Cándido Portinari, among many others.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 00:49:48','2022-09-27 01:45:45'),
(55,5,13,'<b>Reading Campaigns</b>','literatura/leoluegoexisto.jpg','<p>They are made up by the programs Do you want me to read it to you again? (<i>¿Quieres que te lo lea otra vez?</i>) aimed at children and young audiences, and I read... therefore I am! (<i>¡Leo… luego existo!</i>) which focuses on young people, adults, and senior citizens. Their goal is to encourage curiosity, empathy, and an interest in books and literature.</p><p>In 45-minute segments, experienced actors, and actresses (e.g Carlos Bracho, Julieta Egurrola, Odiseo Bichir, Irma Dorantes, Ignacio López Tarso, Cecilia Toussaint, among others) read texts by writers such as Carlos Monsiváis, Rosario Castellanos, José Agustín, Jorge Ibargüengoitia, Elena Poniatowska, Carlos Fuentes, etc. At the end of each segment, a 15-minute dialogue is established between the host and the audience. <br><br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 01:50:01','2022-09-27 03:48:21'),
(56,5,13,'<b>Art Passport <i>(Pasaporte del Arte)</i></b>','literatura/pasaporte.jpg','<p>The program aims at fostering an enjoyment for the arts in all children, with the intent of helping them develop personal aspirations to participate and pursue their interest in art.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 01:52:30','2022-09-27 03:48:31'),
(57,7,14,'<b>Course: Art and Disability: Strengthening Accessible Cultural Institutions</b>','psidi/inclusion.jpg','<p>The course is built around the principles of accessibility and inclusive creations, with an emphasis on the disability social model, and the diversity of the disability community.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 04:36:48','2022-09-27 15:43:00'),
(58,7,14,'<b>Course: A Critique to the Representation of Femininity on Scenic Practices</b>\r\n','psidi/mujer.jpg','<p>The course is built around the principles of accessibility and inclusive creations, with an emphasis on the disability social model, and the diversity of the disability community.</p>\r\n<p>It is based on feminist studies, which are utilized as a toolbox for the analysis of dramatic texts.</p>',1,'2022-09-27 04:38:39','2022-09-27 15:50:39'),
(59,7,14,'<b>Workshop: The Creation of Restorative Scenic Spaces</b>','psidi/comunitaria.jpg','<p>It provides theoretical and practical tools from diverse disciplines such as ethnography, ecology, and epistemologies from the Southern Hemisphere, with the purpose of rethinking and crafting scenic experiences while interacting with the public, contemplating aspects such as kindness and care for our community.<br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 04:40:02','2022-09-27 15:43:18'),
(60,7,14,'<b>Workshop: Community Narratives: Accompaniment for Senior Citizens </b>','psidi/3a.jpg','<p>What are the stories that, throughout our lives, have etched themselves to our bodies and turn us into the individuals we are today?&nbsp; </p><p>Using contemporary dance as a tool, this workshop is aimed at women. It intertwines physical movement with narrative practices, which gives the possibility of collaborating both in individual spaces, and on communities. <br><br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 04:41:16','2022-09-27 15:43:27'),
(61,7,14,'<b>Workshop: Philosophy and Methodology for the Development of Inclusive Cultural Projects</b>','psidi/mujeres.jpg','<p>Coming from a theoretical and practical approach, the aim of this workshop is to promote discussion on diverse topics through a feminist lens and considering inclusion as a social phenomena. <br></p>',1,'2022-09-27 04:42:42','2022-09-27 15:50:00');
